      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nOkay, I've decided on Google Cloud Firestore as the document store for this Python script. Now, I'm figuring out how to structure the `query_documents.py` file to handle queries based on field values or partition keys specifically within this Firestore context. I'm focusing on making the code modular and easily adaptable, keeping the provider explicit and identifiable.\n\n\n**Choosing Firestore for Queries**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the specifics for the `query_documents.py` file. I'm going with Google Cloud Firestore, keeping the provider explicitly identified in the code, for instance with the `google.cloud.firestore` import and calls to the `firestore.Client`. This simplifies querying documents by either a particular field value or partition key.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863069677,
          "start": 1789863067655
        },
