      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Document Storage**\n\nI'm currently focused on the initial setup for `fetch_document.py`. The primary goal is to fetch a document using its ID from a managed NoSQL store. I need to make a choice for the external provider, which is important to make the code identifiable, so the next task is deciding on the specific NoSQL document store to implement.\n\n\n**Selecting DynamoDB Implementation**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS DynamoDB as the managed NoSQL provider for `fetch_document.py`. The plan involves using the `boto3` library, specifically `boto3.client('dynamodb')` or `boto3.resource('dynamodb')` to interact with the database. The core functionality will fetch a document using a provided identifier and table name. Next, I'll start writing the file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863065206,
          "start": 1789863063720
        },
